Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 71/90] Updated structure templates read ahead from one pack
 file

The spawn's structures read thousands of cached template files one at a time, each under a chunk's generation lock: on a slow drive (~0.5 s a file) the other generation threads queued behind it (join samples: HorizonWorldgen.advance BLOCKED on a thread in readCompressed). The templates are kept in one templates.pack, read whole on a background thread at the bridge's start (18-450 ms for 2,881), and served from memory; this run's new ones are added at exit (shutdown hook). Made once from the single files, which stay the fallback.

UMP, 184 mods warm: join 43-48 -> 41 s, ready 84-88 -> 83-84 s.
